    {
      "id": "IOaGy-9hp8nVme0bc3KQ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 920,
      "width": 545.6,
      "height": 660,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aq",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 343838639,
      "version": 3,
      "versionNonce": 899262855,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1795131014887,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "REQUIREMENTS (prompt: the regional LB control plane\nin us-east-1 is down)\nFR\n- Customers can still read their LB configs while the\n  home region's CP is down (may be stale, with as_of)\n- Fail an LB over to a backup region: recreate it from\n  the last replicated config, with backends there\n- HA config per LB: ordered backup regions,\n  MANUAL or AUTO, WARM or COLD standby\n- List regions and their control-plane status\n- Create/update LBs in any healthy region\nOut of scope: LB data-plane internals, replicating\nbackend data (the customer owns state)\n\nNFR\n- CP API 99.99%; survives the loss of 1 region\n- LB writes: strongly consistent, single writer (home);\n  reads: any region, may be stale\n- Failover RTO < 1 min (WARM) / < 10 min (COLD)\n- Config RPO = replication lag, target < 5 s\n- If only the CP is down, existing LBs keep serving:\n  never move traffic just because the CP is down\n\nESTIMATE (all assumptions)\n- 1M LBs, 40% homed in us-east-1 = 400k\n- Normal CP load: 100 writes/s, 5k reads/s\n- Config ~20 KB/LB -> 20 GB total; replication tiny\n- Outage: 10% of 400k fail over in 15 min\n  = 40k creates = ~45 creates/s on us-west-2,\n  ~10x its normal create rate\nPunchline: data is tiny. The problems are a herd of\nfailovers hitting one backup region, and never\nletting two regions own the same LB.",
      "originalText": "REQUIREMENTS (prompt: the regional LB control plane\nin us-east-1 is down)\nFR\n- Customers can still read their LB configs while the\n  home region's CP is down (may be stale, with as_of)\n- Fail an LB over to a backup region: recreate it from\n  the last replicated config, with backends there\n- HA config per LB: ordered backup regions,\n  MANUAL or AUTO, WARM or COLD standby\n- List regions and their control-plane status\n- Create/update LBs in any healthy region\nOut of scope: LB data-plane internals, replicating\nbackend data (the customer owns state)\n\nNFR\n- CP API 99.99%; survives the loss of 1 region\n- LB writes: strongly consistent, single writer (home);\n  reads: any region, may be stale\n- Failover RTO < 1 min (WARM) / < 10 min (COLD)\n- Config RPO = replication lag, target < 5 s\n- If only the CP is down, existing LBs keep serving:\n  never move traffic just because the CP is down\n\nESTIMATE (all assumptions)\n- 1M LBs, 40% homed in us-east-1 = 400k\n- Normal CP load: 100 writes/s, 5k reads/s\n- Config ~20 KB/LB -> 20 GB total; replication tiny\n- Outage: 10% of 400k fail over in 15 min\n  = 40k creates = ~45 creates/s on us-west-2,\n  ~10x its normal create rate\nPunchline: data is tiny. The problems are a herd of\nfailovers hitting one backup region, and never\nletting two regions own the same LB.",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
