      "updated": 1795131014887,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "CORE PATH: failover with a fenced epoch\n-- 1. move ownership (global directory, one txn)\nUPDATE load_balancer\n  SET home_region = :to, epoch = epoch + 1,\n      state = 'FAILING_OVER'\n  WHERE lb_id = :id AND epoch = :seen_epoch\n    AND home_region = :from;\n-- 0 rows -> 409 (already failed over)\nINSERT INTO failover_op(...);   -- same txn\n-- 2. us-west-2 workflow, idempotent on (lb_id, epoch)\ncfg = latest replicated lb_config (version V)\ncreate LB in to-region from cfg, tagged with epoch\nregister targets in to-region; wait until healthy\nflip DNS record only if record.epoch < epoch\nstate = ACTIVE; tell customer \"restored from V\"\n-- 3. us-east-1 comes back\nlocal epoch < directory epoch -> FENCED:\nreject writes; old LB serves until customer decides\n\nDEEP DIVES\n1 Region health: synthetic canaries (describe +\n  create) from 3 other regions, 2-of-3 quorum.\n  Not self-reported: a dead region cannot report.\n2 Router: anycast, stateless, caches directory rows\n  (TTL 5 s). Reads to any replica; writes to home.\n3 Thundering herd: failover admission queue per\n  backup region, priority by tier, quota and\n  capacity reserved for WARM standbys.\n4 Traffic: CP-only outage -> do NOT flip DNS. Flip\n  only if the LB data plane fails too, or on request.\n5 Failback: never automatic; customer runs a planned\n  failover back once us-east-1 is healthy.",
      "originalText": "CORE PATH: failover with a fenced epoch\n-- 1. move ownership (global directory, one txn)\nUPDATE load_balancer\n  SET home_region = :to, epoch = epoch + 1,\n      state = 'FAILING_OVER'\n  WHERE lb_id = :id AND epoch = :seen_epoch\n    AND home_region = :from;\n-- 0 rows -> 409 (already failed over)\nINSERT INTO failover_op(...);   -- same txn\n-- 2. us-west-2 workflow, idempotent on (lb_id, epoch)\ncfg = latest replicated lb_config (version V)\ncreate LB in to-region from cfg, tagged with epoch\nregister targets in to-region; wait until healthy\nflip DNS record only if record.epoch < epoch\nstate = ACTIVE; tell customer \"restored from V\"\n-- 3. us-east-1 comes back\nlocal epoch < directory epoch -> FENCED:\nreject writes; old LB serves until customer decides\n\nDEEP DIVES\n1 Region health: synthetic canaries (describe +\n  create) from 3 other regions, 2-of-3 quorum.\n  Not self-reported: a dead region cannot report.\n2 Router: anycast, stateless, caches directory rows\n  (TTL 5 s). Reads to any replica; writes to home.\n3 Thundering herd: failover admission queue per\n  backup region, priority by tier, quota and\n  capacity reserved for WARM standbys.\n4 Traffic: CP-only outage -> do NOT flip DNS. Flip\n  only if the LB data plane fails too, or on request.\n5 Failback: never automatic; customer runs a planned\n  failover back once us-east-1 is healthy.",
